---
// About page structure (spec 002; the text task T113 moved to spec 005
// with the go-live pause). The visible text below is INTERIM wording
// written from what the project's own documents say about the site —
// no invented biography — and stands in until Erik supplies his own
// words (2026-09-19: he asked for a stand-in for now). T113 stays open
// in specs/005-going-live/spec.md; this comment is the only marker.
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/url';
import { t } from '../../i18n';
---

<BaseLayout title={t('about.title')} description="About Erik Haake.">
  <section class="page-head section">
    <p class="eyebrow">{t('about.eyebrow')}</p>
    <h1>Erik Haake</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Photographer. This site is where the photographs are written up: pieces about a day out with a
      camera, the frames it produced, and what stayed with me afterwards.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Profile</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-stack">
      <p>
        Most of the work is landscape and nature, with street, portrait, and event photography
        alongside. Rather than a feed, the site is organised as pieces: each one pairs a set of
        images with the writing that belongs to them, whether that is an account of an outing, notes
        on gear, or a short announcement.
      </p>
      <p>
        The galleries collect images by category and link back to the piece each came from. Every
        photograph has its own page with the exposure it was made at.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose-grid about-closing">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Reach me</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-stack">
      <p>
        The <a href={withBase('/contact/')}>contact page</a> has email and Instagram.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
